course: dictionary
lesson: 11613
title: Caught by the police: apprehended
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Apprehended is a formal word, often used in news reports and police language. It is the past form of apprehend. «The police apprehended the thief outside the bank.» The clues are police and thief, so apprehended means caught and arrested.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The police caught the thief outside the bank» still makes sense, so you are right. Look for the clues around the word: who did it, and what happened next.
explain: Apprehended has a second meaning, understood, but it is rare and mostly found in old books. In everyday reading and news, the meaning to remember is caught and arrested.
fact: Apprehend means to catch and arrest someone, usually the police doing it.
fact: «Apprehended» is the past form: «The police apprehended the suspect yesterday.»
fact: A «suspect» is a person the police think may have done a crime.
fact: Common phrases are «be apprehended by police» and «apprehended the suspect».
fact: In rare, old-fashioned writing, apprehended can mean understood, but you will mostly meet the police meaning.
exercise: «The police apprehended the thief outside the bank.» What does apprehended mean? | Chased away from the bank | Given a prize for good work | Lost in the crowd | *Caught and arrested by the police
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The suspect was apprehended after a short chase.» that means a person thought to have done a crime. | chase | short | *suspect | after
exercise: «Two officers apprehended the man who had stolen the bike.» Which word could swap in for apprehended without changing the meaning? | thanked | painted | lost | *arrested
test: «The thief was apprehended by police early in the morning.» What does apprehended mean here? | Shouted at loudly | Given a reward | *Caught and arrested | Forgotten about
test: Which phrase means about the same as «apprehended the suspect»? | Painted the suspect | Lost the suspect | *Caught the suspect | Thanked the suspect
exam: Which sentence shows that someone was caught and arrested? | *The officers apprehended the robber on the motorway. | The officers cooked the robber a meal. | The officers praised the robber for his good manners. | The officers painted the robber's car red.
